  "methods": {
    "endpoints": "Score each of 30 consecutive native camera observations, with measured endpoints 3.001000, 3.001999, 3.022000 and 3.001000 seconds. Models use the trained nominal 0.1-second discretization.",
    "coordinates": "Per-frame released 3D centre transformed to common world coordinates and expressed in the virtual LiDAR XY frame at the final historical timestamp. Roadside cameras supply 5 original frames and annotated tracks. Parent checkpoints trained on fixed PINNS cameras using 2D top-down ground observations.",
    "inputs": "Sensor observations are oracle-associated by released historical boxes, local ID and metric centre. Annotation timing is documented; trajectories and crops are released offline. No independent online detector for this comparison. Image joints are estimated, not ground-truth keypoints. Standing is assigned from the last observed nominal-step speed below 0.20 m/s. The PINNS-specific source standing flag is unavailable.",
    "estimand": "Four held-out-PINNS checkpoint errors equally weighted before pooling four distinct windows and two distinct people. No inference to additional people/sites. Primary zero-degree M1 minus M0 ADE. All rotations prespecified, no selection. Network uses fixed 0.1s discretization; measured clock separately reported for every case.",
    "uncertainty": "Single illustrative official example, two people, one person contributes three of four windows. No population confidence interval.",
    "label_provenance": "The authors describe per-frame cuboid labels with sequence IDs that can persist during complete occlusion. Explicit temporal interpolation in Sec. 3.1 concerns cross-view cooperative alignment. Here the infrastructure camera-exposure label stream is used; its rows do not certify independent manual measurements per frame.",
    "observed_crop_annotation_occluded_state_counts": {
      "0": 7,
      "1": 12,
      "2": 1
    }
  },
